               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nAlthough it is rarely used (<htcite0>), the cosecant deserves its place among the trigonometric functions. In this text we reviewed that csc(θ) = 1 / sin(θ): it equals 1 when sin(θ) = 1, grows as sin(θ) shrinks, and has no value where sin(θ) = 0 — the same behavior **Graph 3** and our interactive figure make visible.",
